--TEST--
An `@param` or `@return` whose sentence starts with the declared type is `E0332`, and `null` on a nullable parameter is not — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A tag's sentence does not start by repeating the declared type.
// `null` on a `?string` parameter says when it is null, so it is allowed.
final class Ledger {
    /// Adds one entry.
    ///
    /// @param $amount int amount to add
    /// @param $note null when there is no note
    /// @return int the new total
    public static function add(int $amount, ?string $note): int {
        return $amount;
    }
}
echo Ledger::add(3, null), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0332]: `@param` repeats the type `int`
  --> %s:7:24
  |
7 |     /// @param $amount int amount to add
  |                        ^^^ the type is in the signature
  = suggestion: delete `int` (delete)

error[E0332]: `@return` repeats the type `int`
  --> %s:9:17
  |
9 |     /// @return int the new total
  |                 ^^^ the type is in the signature
  = suggestion: delete `int` (delete)

error: aborting due to 2 errors
